",\n  \"then\": \"The screen displays the retained submitted assumption values and the forecast response associated with those values, using the configured default gain rate.\",\n  \"when\": \"A user opens the forecast and edits either assumption before requesting a refreshed forecast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"The forecast response contains a feeding adjustment or sale-timing recommendation.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n  \"level\": \"ui\",\n  \"then\": \"The screen displays the returned recommendation and any associated ADG, projected market date, or plan-variance values supplied with it.\",\n  \"when\": \"A user views the lot forecast or insights.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"Inventory responses contain feed items and stock movements.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n  \"level\": \"ui\",\n  \"then\": \"The screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, wastage-entered, and closing stock values as available.\",\n  \"when\": \"A user opens inventory details and movement history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A user enters actual wastage as a stock movement.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n  \"level\": \"ui\",\n  \"then\": \"The screen displays the returned actual-wastage movement separately from consumption estimates and the configured wastage ratio.\",\n  \"when\": \"The movement is saved and the user opens the movement history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"A user has configured a wastage ratio and the inventory response contains projected balances.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n  \"level\": \"ui\",\n  \"then\": \"The screen displays the returned daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual projected balances reflecting the selected ratio in consumption estimates, with each horizon labeled and no low-stock alert shown.\",\n  \"when\": \"The user selects each supported forecast horizon.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"approved-screens\" kind=\"approved-screens\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"screen\": \"S-2\",\n  \"route\": \"/imports\",\n  \"reqs\": [\n   \"REQ-1\",\n   \"REQ-2\",\n   \"REQ-19\",\n   \"REQ-21\"\n  ],\n  \"states\": [\n   \"Preview loaded with returned row outcomes and proposed lot links.\",\n   \"Sync result with added, already-present, duplicate, pending-mapping, capacity-blocked, and failed counts; partial results must not be labeled complete.\",\n   \"Validation error when a supplied file cannot be previewed.\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Import records\",\n  \"buttons\": [\n   \"Preview records\"\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n   \"Source file selection / batch selector\"\n  ],\n  \"columns\": [],\n  \"messages\": {},\n  \"toasts\": []\n },\n {\n  \"screen\": \"S-3\",\n  \"route\": \"/lots-pens\",\n  \"reqs\": [\n   \"REQ-2\",\n   \"REQ-3\",\n   \"REQ-14\",\n   \"REQ-21\"\n  ],\n  \"states\": [\n   \"Validation when target weight or default gain rate is invalid.\",\n   \"Saved lot assumptions with recalculated forecast.\",\n   \"Unresolved lot or receipt shown as unavailable for pen operations.\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Lots & pens\",\n  \"buttons\": [\n   \"Save lot assumptions\"\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n   \"Search lot or pen\",\n   \"Target weight (lb)\",\n   \"Default gain rate (lb/day)\"\n  ],\n  \"columns\": [\n   \"Lot\",\n   \"Pen\",\n   \"Head\",\n   \"Breed & Sex\",\n   \"PO Line Trace\",\n   \"Status\"\n  ],\n  \"messages\": {},\n  \"toasts\": []\n },\n {\n  \"screen\": \"S-4\",\n  \"route\": \"/inventory\",\n  \"reqs\": [\n   \"REQ-4\",\n   \"REQ-21\"\n  ],\n  \"states\": [\n   \"Movement form validation.\",\n   \"Movement saved and reflected in the item balance.\",\n   \"Actual wastage saved separately from ordinary stock movement.\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Feed inventory\",\n  \"buttons\": [\n   \"Save movement\",\n   \"Record actual wastage\"\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n   \"Feed item\",\n   \"Movement type\",\n   \"Date (America/Denver)\",\n   \"Quantity (lb)\",\n   \"Note\",\n   \"Commodity item\",\n   \"Record date\",\n   \"Actual wastage (lb)\",\n   \"Wastage cause / notes\"\n  ],\n  \"columns\": [\n   \"Feed item\",\n   \"Unit price\",\n   \"Current stock\",\n   \"Annual outlook\",\n   \"Status\"\n  ],\n  \"messages\": {},\n  \"toasts\": []\n },\n {\n  \"screen\": \"S-5\",\n  \"route\": \"/inventory/outlook\",\n  \"reqs\": [\n   \"REQ-5\",\n   \"REQ-21\"\n  ],\n  \"states\": [\n   \"Projection recalculates immediately after a wastage ratio change.\",\n   \"Validation for an out-of-range wastage ratio.\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Inventory outlook\",\n  \"buttons\": [],\n  \"fields\": [],\n  \"columns\": [\n   \"Feed commodity\",\n   \"Current stock\",\n   \"Daily est.\",\n   \"Daily balance\",\n   \"Annual balance\"\n  ],\n  \"messages\": {},\n  \"toasts\": []\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"stubs\" kind=\"stubs\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"path\": \"lib/feed-to-gain-calculator.ts\",\n  \"content\": \"export type FeedUnit = \\\"lb\\\" | \\\"kg\\\" | \\\"ton\\\";\\n\\nexport interface FeedToGainEvent {\\n  quantity: number;\\n  unit: FeedUnit;\\n  cost: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FeedToGainInput {\\n  receivingDate: string;\\n  asOfDate: string;\\n  entryAverageWeightLb: number;\\n  currentAverageWeightLb: number;\\n  entryHeadcount: number;\\n  currentHeadcount: number;\\n  feedingEvents: FeedToGainEvent[];\\n  targetWeightLb: number;\\n  defaultAdgLbPerDay: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface FeedToGainResult {\\n  daysOnFeed: number;\\n  totalGainLb: number;\\n  averageDailyGainLbPerDay: number | null;\\n  totalFeedAsFedLb: number;\\n  feedConversionRatio: number | null;\\n  feedCostPerPoundOfGain: number | null;\\n  projectedMarketDate: string | null;\\n}\\n\\nexport class FeedToGainCalculator {\\n  static calculate(_input: FeedToGainInput): FeedToGainResult {\\n    throw new Error(\\\"not implemented\\\");\\n  }\\n}\\n\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<pointers>\n- contracts/openapi.yaml: the locked API contract; the client and test handlers in lib/api are generated from it\n</pointers>\n\nWrite the acceptance and characterisation tests now.\nBefore you return, check your list against the criteria: each of these needs at least one test in it: AC-1.1, AC-1.2, AC-2.1, AC-2.2, AC-2.3, AC-3.1, AC-3.2, AC-3.3, AC-4.1, AC-4.2, AC-5.1.\nThis session is cut off after 60 turns, 45 minutes or about $2 of model use, whichever comes first, and you are not warned. Long tool output, whole-file rewrites and reading a file again all use it up. Write every test first, then check them.\n\n<recap>\n- one test per AC\n- tests fail now for the right reason\n- characterisation tests pass today\n- don't touch production code\n</recap>"}